</name><name><surname>King</surname><given-names>RA</given-names></name><name><surname>Ferris</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Ayres</surname><given-names>DR</given-names></name><name><surname>Strong</surname><given-names>DR</given-names></name><article-title>Reciprocal hybrid formation of <italic>Spartina </italic>in San Francisco Bay</article-title><source>Mol Ecol</source><year>2000</year><volume>9</volume><fpage>765</fpage><lpage>770</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1046/j.1365-294x.2000.00935.x</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10849292</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="B19"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><name><surname>Peng</surname><given-names>CI</given-names></name><name><surname>Chiang</surname><given-names>TY</given-names></name><article-title>Molecular confirmation of unidirectional hybridization in <italic>Begonia </italic>&#x000d7; <italic>taipeiensis </italic>Peng (Begoniaceae) from Taiwan</article-title><source>Ann Missouri Bot Gard</source><year>2000</year><volume>87</volume><fpage>273</fpage><lpage>285</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.2307/2666164</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="B20"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><name><surname>Moody</surname><given-names>ML</given-names></name><name><surname>Les</surname><given-names>DH</given-names></name><article-title>Evidence of hybridity in invasive water milfoil (<italic>Myriophyllum</italic>) populations</article-title><source>Proc Natl Acad Sci USA</source><year>2002</year><volume>99</volume><fpage>14867</fpage><lpage>14871</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1073/pnas.172391499</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12407174</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="B21"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><name><surname>Bleeker</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name><article-title>Hybridization and <italic>Rorippa austriaca </italic>(Brassicaceae) invasion in Germany</article-title><source>Mol Ecol</source><year>2003</year><volume>12</volume><fpage>1831</fpage><lpage>1841</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1046/j.1365-294X.2003.01854.x</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12803635</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="B22"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><name><surname>Fant</surname><given-names>JB</given-names></name><name><surname>Kamau</surname><given-names>EM</given-names></name><name><surname>Preston</surname><given-names>CD</given-names></name><article-title>Chloroplast evidence for the multiple origins of the hybrid <italic>Potamogeton </italic>&#x000d7; <italic>sudermanicus </italic>Hagstr</article-title><source>Aquat Bot</source><year>2003</year><volume>75</volume><fpage>351</fpage><lpage>356</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/S0304-3770(03)00004-4</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="B23"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><name><surname>Taberlet</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Gielly</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Pautou</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Bouvet</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><article-title>Universal primers for amplification of three non-coding regions of chloroplast DNA</article-title><source>Plant Mol Biol</source><year>1991</year><volume>17</volume><fpage>1105</fpage><lpage>1109</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1007/BF00037152</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">1932684</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="B24"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><name><surname>Gielly</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Taberlet</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><article-title>The use of chloroplast DNA to resolve plant phylogenies: noncoding versus <italic>rbc </italic>L sequences</article-title><source>Mol Biol Evol</source><year>1994</year><volume>11</volume><fpage>769</fpage><lpage>777</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7968490</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="B25"><mixed-citation publication-type="jo